# The `.claude/` capability layer IS this repo — skills, hooks, agents,
# registries and capability routing are all tracked. A blanket `.claude` rule
# lived here until 2026-07-31 and silently excluded every one of them; do not
# reintroduce it. Ignore individual machine-local paths below instead.

# Hook run logs: append-only local side effects, and they capture prompt text
# and transcript paths, so they must never be committed.
.claude/hooks/*.log

# Machine-local: which project MCP servers this machine has approved.
# Belongs to the checkout, not the repo.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Hook state: per-turn and per-review bookkeeping, rewritten constantly and
# meaningful only to this checkout. Tracking it churns every commit, and worse,
# `05-docs-gate.py` counts changed files that are not knowledge docs -- so a
# tracked marker makes the gate partly trigger on its own bookkeeping.
# `review-receipts.json` was tracked until 2026-08-02 and its writes changed the
# fingerprint it had just recorded, so no receipt ever survived; see
# ISSUES.md 2026-08-01 21:15.
.claude/hooks/state/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
